      "skills": "Planning and carrying out a food test safely, recording results in a table (building on Lesson 2), comparing test results with Table 1 data, constructing an explanation from evidence, and revising a model.",
      "attitudes": "Curiosity about everyday foods, care and responsibility when handling reagents, respect for the ideas of group members, and appreciation of locally available protein foods such as beans, milk and omena.",
