      "skills": "Planning a fair test and controlling variables; using the iodine test and Benedict's test; measuring time; calculating relative rate = 60 / time in seconds; drawing and interpreting line graphs; using data as evidence for an explanation (NGSS practices: planning and carrying out investigations, analysing and interpreting data, constructing explanations).",
      "attitudes": "Curiosity about everyday food experiences; honesty in recording results; teamwork and respect for others' ideas in groups of 4; appreciation that traditional Kenyan foods work with the chemistry of the body.",
