        "teacherMoves": "Say: 'Which of our earlier questions can we now answer with evidence from today?' WAIT TIME of 10-15 seconds. Cold-call 3 groups to move a note and justify using a number from Table 3. Ask: 'What new question has this lesson created that we will need for Lesson 6?' Collect at least 4 new questions and group them into 'enzymes', 'food and energy' and 'meals'. Praise questions that are testable.",
        "sensemakingStrategy": "Driving Question Board as a public record of growing understanding: moving answered questions and adding new ones makes the learning trail visible and ties each lesson back to the phenomenon.",
        "formativeAssessment": "Check that sticky notes are specific and testable rather than 'What is an enzyme?'. At least one question per group should connect enzymes to the athlete's diet. Note which learners cite evidence when moving a question to 'answered'."
