      "knowledge": "Learners will explain that a plate of ugali, beans, sukuma wiki and milk is not plain: it contains carbohydrates (starch in maize, supplying and storing energy as glucose and glycogen), proteins (beans, milk, omena; amino acids for growth and repair, and enzymes) and lipids (milk fat, groundnuts, cooking oil; stored energy and insulation). They will use Energy = 4 x C + 4 x P + 9 x F to compare Meals A, B and C and explain that enzymes such as amylase, working best at about 37 C and near neutral pH, break big food molecules into small ones the body can absorb.",
      "skills": "Analysing and interpreting data (NGSS SEP 4): calculating and comparing energy and energy shares. Engaging in argument from evidence (SEP 7): writing a Claim-Evidence-Reasoning statement. Constructing explanations (SEP 6): giving the final explanation of the phenomenon. Developing and using models (SEP 2): comparing the Lesson 1 model with the final model. Communication and collaboration in groups of 4.",
